+# Direct Metal 4 render passes on NVN2
+
+The first guest command list selects the policy using the NPDM platform, the hosted 16-digit title ID and the active queue. The default enables the proven rules for NVN2 titles including `0400C3F00006E000`. `S2A_RB_NVN2_TILE_PASSES=0` restores the previous generic path. The legacy `04007EF01F8AE000` target retains its 810/811 settings. An unidentified session, NVN1 and Metal 3 retain the previous path. Set flags before launch.
+
+| Control | Rule |
+| --- | --- |
+| `S2A_RB_GPU_CLEAR_STORES=0` | Disable generic store elision. The enabled rule requires a whole matching subresource that will actually be cleared before an observer in this command buffer. A sealed list can supply the proof only across END transitions within the submitted piece. |
+| `S2A_RB_GPU_ATTACHMENT_LIVENESS=0` | Disable traversal across sealed lists and the private-clear exception for heap alias visibility. Direct full-overwrite and clear-batch candidates still require a non-overlapping descriptor and virtual backing history. |
+| `S2A_RB_GPU_PRODUCER=0` | Disable generic consumer-barrier elision. The proof is an immediately preceding full producer in the same queue and command buffer. A relaxed producer, wait, submission cut or foreign encoder invalidates the proof. Placement heaps retain alias visibility unless a clear-only pass has exclusively unexposed private attachments. The existing explicit `DM_NVN_PRODUCER_COVER` override takes precedence. |
+| `S2A_RB_GPU_CLEAR_BATCH=0` | Keep the original adjacent pending clear groups. The enabled rule validates physical storage, formats, extent, slots and load/store actions before joining two groups at their original materialization point. |
+| `S2A_RB_GPU_PASS_STATS=1` | Count barrier reasons and classify every pass attachment. These detailed counters are off by default on the generic path. |
+
+An overlapping descriptor, virtual mapping, invalid range or saturated history keeps the conservative store/batch decision. Histories start before the first replay and remain valid until session shutdown. Attachment bytes in the host log are logical bytes. Use GPU counters for DRAM traffic and device measurements for energy and thermals.
+
+Run `make native-test-rb_clear_batch_metal` with the project's native-test makefile on macOS. The target checks original behavior, the new title with the master disabled and the default-enabled title in separate processes. On a physical Metal 4 system the fixture submits NVN commands, checks selected store actions through their counters, exercises actual producer coverage and clear fusion, and reads every pixel of both attachments. On virtual Macs lacking a Metal 4 queue and residency set it applies the shared clear/alias proof to tracked Metal passes and reads both textures, including the untouched attachment. This fallback leaves direct-queue barrier and replay coverage for a capable GPU.
